WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.391 --> 00:00:03.141
(dramatic music)

00:00:06.962 --> 00:00:11.156
- The average visitor in Napa
doesn't look at vineyards

00:00:11.156 --> 00:00:13.073
and think of barn owls.

00:00:15.801 --> 00:00:18.528
They think of wine and wine-tasting,

00:00:18.528 --> 00:00:22.611
but owls are really a part
of this whole process.

00:00:24.580 --> 00:00:27.981
Walking up to an owl box and
hearing the babies hissing

00:00:27.981 --> 00:00:29.690
is pretty scary sounding.

00:00:29.690 --> 00:00:32.273
(owls hissing)

00:00:33.242 --> 00:00:36.938
And then you just pull out
this little fluffy owl.

00:00:36.938 --> 00:00:41.105
They're gonna grow up to be
rodent devouring machines.

00:00:46.605 --> 00:00:48.847
(gentle upbeat music)

00:00:48.847 --> 00:00:52.569
My name is Carrie Wendt;
I'm a wildlife biologist.

00:00:52.569 --> 00:00:54.186
I've spent the last couple years

00:00:54.186 --> 00:00:57.570
driving around visiting
hundreds of owl boxes

00:00:57.570 --> 00:01:00.032
on 65 vineyards in Napa Valley

00:01:00.032 --> 00:01:02.669
to better understand how barn owls

00:01:02.669 --> 00:01:04.836
and vineyards can coexist.

00:01:06.718 --> 00:01:10.082
Without owls, the rodent
population would explode

00:01:10.082 --> 00:01:12.642
and they would cause a lot
more damage to vineyards.

00:01:12.642 --> 00:01:15.104
Here's a couple of skulls
I pulled out of the box.

00:01:15.104 --> 00:01:17.589
This is proof that they're eating rodents.

00:01:17.589 --> 00:01:21.582
Using barn owls to reduce
rodent populations on vineyards

00:01:21.582 --> 00:01:24.033
is the alternative way to kill rodents.

00:01:24.033 --> 00:01:26.485
Grow up to be big and strong.

00:01:26.485 --> 00:01:28.308
Eat lots of gophers.

00:01:28.308 --> 00:01:30.252
The mainstream, conventional
way of killing rodents

00:01:30.252 --> 00:01:32.150
is to apply rodenticides.

00:01:32.150 --> 00:01:33.648
Rodenticides are really harmful

00:01:33.648 --> 00:01:37.086
so using owls is
definitely the sustainable

00:01:37.086 --> 00:01:39.555
eco-friendly way to reduce rodents.

00:01:39.555 --> 00:01:41.557
(owl hissing)

00:01:41.557 --> 00:01:43.276
You have to have a special
permit to hand these bands

00:01:43.276 --> 00:01:45.082
and to be able to band birds.

00:01:45.082 --> 00:01:46.693
Each band is an individual number,

00:01:46.693 --> 00:01:49.277
so it's an individual
identification for that one bird

00:01:49.277 --> 00:01:51.620
that won't ever be on a different bird.

00:01:51.620 --> 00:01:54.512
My colleagues are currently using GPS tags

00:01:54.512 --> 00:01:58.238
and motion-detecting cameras
to paint a fuller picture

00:01:58.238 --> 00:02:00.154
of how barn owls may provide

00:02:00.154 --> 00:02:02.321
pest control services in vineyards.

00:02:02.321 --> 00:02:06.321
We're banding them to see
where they're nesting.

00:02:07.322 --> 00:02:12.273
When we capture the adult birds
to put GPS trackers on them,

00:02:12.273 --> 00:02:14.341
we want them to stay as calm as possible,

00:02:14.341 --> 00:02:16.753
so we put an adorable hat over their eyes.

00:02:16.753 --> 00:02:18.920
You wanna put that on her?

00:02:20.189 --> 00:02:24.356
We found this silly owl hat
and we thought it was perfect.

00:02:25.892 --> 00:02:28.211
There's so many opportunities
for vineyard owners

00:02:28.211 --> 00:02:31.446
to enhance wildlife
habitat on their vineyards

00:02:31.446 --> 00:02:33.311
that's mutually beneficial.

00:02:33.311 --> 00:02:36.142
And I think providing barn owl nest boxes

00:02:36.142 --> 00:02:38.086
on vineyards is a perfect example

00:02:38.086 --> 00:02:40.035
of how that relationship can flourish.

00:02:40.035 --> 00:02:43.202
(gentle upbeat music)

